From de60887b64415a4eec74651bda019fc5d3c580d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 04:56:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] feat(registry): add a status subresource write

ReconcileResult.status_patch had nowhere to go: put() rewrites the whole
object, so a controller writing status through it would race with spec
writers and could not leave generation alone.

Add update_status(kind, namespace, name, tenant_id, status_patch, *,
observed_generation, expected_version). It merges conditions by type
(status.conditions for payloads with a status subtree, top-level
conditions otherwise), refreshes lastTransitionTime only when a
condition's status changes, validates an optional phase against the
kind's state machine, records observedGeneration, and never touches spec
or generation. It edits the stored JSON so payload fields the registry
does not model are preserved, compares-and-swaps on resource_version when
asked to, skips the write entirely when nothing changed, and records a
"status" change.
